<title>SWITZERLAND: ACI says Memphis top world cargo airport in Jan-No.</title>
<headline>ACI says Memphis top world cargo airport in Jan-No.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis, base of U.S. express freight carrier, Federal Express, was the world's busiest cargo airport in January-November 1996, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI).</p>
<p>The airport handled 1,751,080 tonnes of cargo in the period in question, up 12.2 percent on January- November 1995.</p>
<p>Occupying second-place in the ACI table of top cargo-handling airports was Los Angeles as a result of reporting 1,567,775 tonnes, up 9.3 percent on the previous year's levels.</p>
<p>In third place was Miami, which handled  1,560,698 tonnes, an increase of 8.8 percent on the first eleven months of 1995.</p>
<p>The world's 20 busiest cargo airports in January-November 1996, with the volume they handled, the percentage change over January-November 1995 and, in parentheses, their January-November 1995 ranking, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1   (1)  Memphis		 1,751,080 tonnes   (up 12.2 pct)</p>
<p> 2   (4)  Los Angeles	   1,567,775 tonnes   (up  9.3)</p>
<p> 3   (5)  Miami		   1,560,698 tonnes   (up  8.8)</p>
<p> 4   (3)  New York		1,494,922 tonnes   (up  2.6)</p>
<p> 5   (2)  Tokyo-Narita	  1,479,360 tonnes (down  3.0)</p>
<p> 6   (6)  Hong Kong	     1,442,587 tonnes   (up  6.6)</p>
<p> 7   (7)  Frankfurt	     1,365,014  tonnes  (up  2.5)</p>
<p> 8   (8)  Louisville	    1,256,257 tonnes   (up  1.8)</p>
<p> 9  (10)  Seoul		   1,232,325 tonnes   (up 11.3)</p>
<p> 10 (14)  Anchorage	     1,167,400 tonnes   (up 30.6)</p>
<p> 11  (9)  Chicago		 1,143,394 tonnes   (up  1.4)</p>
<p> 12 (12)  Singapore	     1,098,228  tonnes  (up  7.1)</p>
<p> 13 (11)  London Heathrow     1,044,923  tonnes  (up  1.5)</p>
<p> 14 (13)  Amsterdam	     1,020,019 tonnes   (up 10.7)</p>
<p> 15 (16)  Paris-CDG		 891,926 tonnes   (up  4.5)</p>
<p> 16 (15)  New York Newark	 876,987 tonnes   (up  1.6)</p>
<p> 17 (18)  Atlanta		   728,421 tonnes   (up  4.4)</p>
<p> 18 (19) Taipei		     720,240 tonnes   (up  5.0)</p>
<p> 19 (17)  Dallas Fort Worth     717,230  tonnes  (up  1.0)</p>
<p> 20 (-)  Dayton		     667,782 tonnes   (up 16.1)</p>
